        "original_id": "af8fdb2c-a835-5ee0-806b-b6d585e07292",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Harriet O'Neill, Debra Lehrmann, Rick Green, Rick Perry\n- Roles: judge, family court jurist, state legislator, constitutional speaker, governor\n- Places: Fort Worth, Dripping Springs, Texas\n- Events: April 13 Republican runoff election, appointment to fill a term\n\nFacts:\n- Rick Perry served as the 47th Governor of Texas from December 2000 to January 2015.\n- In the April 13 Republican runoff election, Judge Debra Lehrmann, a family court jurist from Fort Worth, defeated Rick Green, a former state legislator and constitutional speaker from Dripping Springs.\n- Rick Perry appointed Debra Lehrmann to fill out Harriet O'Neill's term.",
